# Spiral — ~1500 Skia circles laid on a logarithmic spiral; every tap springs all of them (one frame-callback spring array) to a spiral with a new random angle.
# What this test covers: first retarget from rest, letting a 3 s spring settle completely, retargeting mid-flight
# (inertia kept/dropped per coordinate and per-element stiffness re-solve), a rapid tap burst that re-solves thousands
# of springs per frame, taps in the corners of the full-screen pressable, and a final settle before closing.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/spiral"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 2500
# Retarget from rest, then let the 3 s spring come fully to rest.
press 200 500
wait 3500
# Retarget mid-flight: half a second into the spring.
press 200 450
wait 500
press 120 300
wait 1200
# Rapid burst: every tap re-solves the stiffness for elements caught mid-flight.
press 200 600 --count 6 --interval-ms 120
wait 800
# Corners of the full-screen pressable.
press 100 835
wait 300
press 370 820
wait 300
press 370 200
wait 3500
press 200 437
wait 3500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
